<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hendrik Carloff</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hendrik Carloff was a merchant and colonial agent of the 17th century who served several companies on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a>. For the Swedish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> Company he obtained land from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fante">Fante</a> rulers and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-coast-castle">Fort Carolusborg</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-coast">Cape Coast</a> in 1653. In 1658 he returned in Danish service and seized the Swedish forts, beginning the Danish Gold Coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hendrik-carloff.jpg" alt="Hendrik Carloff" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FortsGoldk%C3%BCste.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
